@startuml workspace_access_sequence
title OpenCRM — organization workspace access

autonumber
actor "Organization member" as User
boundary "Workspace API" as Api
control "WorkspaceAccessService" as Access
control "OrganizationPermissionService" as Permissions
control "OrganizationEntitlementReader" as Entitlements
control "CRM module service" as Module
database "Main PostgreSQL" as Db

User -> Api : request workspace operation
Api -> Access : authorize organization operation
Access -> Db : load active organization and membership
Db --> Access : roleCode / no membership
alt Organization missing or membership absent
  Access --> Api : deny
  Api --> User : 403 / not found
else Membership exists
  Access -> Permissions : resolve role defaults + explicit overrides
  Permissions -> Db : load organization permissions
  Db --> Permissions : granted / denied
  alt Required permission absent
    Permissions --> Access : deny
    Access --> Api : deny
    Api --> User : 403 Forbidden
  else Permission granted
    Permissions --> Access : allow
    Access -> Entitlements : resolve workspace entitlement
    alt Commercial mode disabled (default)
      Entitlements -> Entitlements : do not query a subscription plan
      Entitlements --> Access : base workspace features
    else Commercial mode enabled
      Entitlements -> Db : load subscription, plan, limits, and features
      Db --> Entitlements : commercial entitlement
      Entitlements --> Access : plan-based access
    end
    alt Write or requested feature is allowed
      Access --> Api : authorized
      Api -> Module : execute operation
      Module -> Db : persist CRM changes
      Db --> Module : committed result
      Module --> Api : result DTO
      Api --> User : 200 / 201
    else Read-only or feature/limit restriction
      Access --> Api : deny operation
      Api --> User : access restriction
    end
  end
end

note over Access,Entitlements
  Membership and role permissions are always enforced.
  Commercial mode adds plan-based restrictions; it does not replace authorization.
end note

@enduml
